  "summary": "Malicious code in bjm-low-code-components (npm)",
  "details": "\n---\n_-= Per source details. Do not edit below this line.=-_\n\n## Source: amazon-inspector (f47bf808132c7ac7ba3324f1e4dec6932c64eabb78e1030ce613267ea9a3cf5b)\nOn npm install, the package's postinstall hook runs canary.js, which collects the installer's hostname, username, current working directory, and selected environment variables and POSTs them over plain HTTP to a hardcoded Burp Collaborator OAST subdomain at 2pslbvbc3adfni1pbe9xy2b1asgj4cs1.oastify.com/bjm-canary. This is a dependency-confusion / reconnaissance beacon: installer-side identity and environment data leave the machine automatically on install to an attacker-controlled endpoint.\n",
